# Laziness proof: a seq whose tail thunk holds a live binding is not forced
# beyond what is consumed by $take.
# `trap` is a binding that raises; it is reachable only from the third element
# of `err-seq`, which `take 2` never demands. The result is the two-element
# collect; `trap` and the third seq element are never evaluated.
[
  trap:    [raise "live binding past n must not be forced"]
  err-seq: [seq 10 [seq 20 [seq trap []]]]
]
[result: [collect [take 2 err-seq]]]
=== error
[E080] live binding past n must not be forced
